    <statement><p>Estimate <m>f(-1.99,1.01)</m> given that <m>f(-2,1)=5, f_x(-2,1)=-2</m> and <m>f_y(-2,1)=-3</m>.</p>
<p><m>f(-1.99,1.01) \approx</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>4.95</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>f</m> at the point <m>(-2,1)</m>, which is
<me>f(-2+h,1+k)\approx f(-2,1)+f_x(-2,1)h+f_y(-2,1)k</me>
Substituting the given values and <m>h=0.01, k=0.01</m> we obtain the following approximation
<me>f(-1.99,1.01)\approx 5  - 2 \cdot (0.01)  - 3 \cdot (0.01)=4.95</me>





</solution>
